  "result": "The rule and its witnesses for `NRS_484B_363_1` are written, and the gate returned **OK** on the first of the 6 allowed runs, with 14 witnesses passing.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_363_1.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject belongs to the `DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle` aggregate.\n- **When it applies:** some school zone sign that isn't an end sign governs a travel region the subject occupies. For that sign and region, none of the four exceptions holds:\n  - (a) it is not a school day;\n  - (b) it is within the half-hour margin outside school operation;\n  - (c) a working beacon covers the zone, pupils are in class, and no working beacon is flashing;\n  - (d) no working beacon covers the zone and the sign's posted conditions don't hold now.\n- **The duty:** speed is at most 15 mph, written with `Units.mph 15`.\n- **Readings:** none of my own. The node already says the duty applies if any sign-and-region pair qualifies, and that \"not flashing\" is checked against every working beacon.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_363_1.lean`): the 8 planned scenarios, plus 6 I added so that every part of the formula changes at least one verdict:\n- the half-hour margin assumption is true (not applicable);\n- pupils are not in class (violated);\n- the beacon is inoperative, once outside the sign's posted hours (not applicable) and once inside them (violated);\n- the zone sign is an end sign (not applicable);\n- the zone sign is a speed zone instead of a school zone (not applicable).\n\nIn `branch_2` I set the time outside the sign's posted hours. That way, exception (d) is ruled out only because a working beacon covers the zone.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
